# Two downloads from one repository.
#
# The users' download - GitHub's "Download ZIP", a release's source archive, git archive - is ChartLibre alone:
# everything marked export-ignore below stays out of it. A developer clones the repository and has it all,
# dev/ (tests, tools, packs' sources, ChartLibre Developer) included.
# The same split as dev/tools/build_bundle.py's packages (wanted_file): keep the two lists alike.

# For developers only. A folder marked export-ignore is not even looked into, so the way down to the two files
# the application uses (dev/tools/launcher/chartlibre.png, docs/manual/user_manual.pdf) stays open: at each
# level everything else is left out, that one folder or file kept.
dev/* export-ignore
dev/tools -export-ignore
dev/tools/* export-ignore
dev/tools/launcher -export-ignore
dev/tools/launcher/* export-ignore
dev/tools/launcher/chartlibre.png -export-ignore
docs/* export-ignore
docs/manual -export-ignore
docs/manual/* export-ignore
docs/manual/user_manual.pdf -export-ignore
todo.txt export-ignore
CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
.github export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
.gitignore export-ignore
pyrightconfig.json export-ignore

# The Windows launchers keep their CRLF line ends on every system.
*.bat text eol=crlf
